- So Mike, is this St. Cloud?

1333
00:46:54,000 --> 00:46:55,567
(Chuckling)

1334
00:46:55,567 --> 00:46:56,567
- That's two.

1335
00:46:56,567 --> 00:46:57,133
- Because it's clouds.

1336
00:47:01,633 --> 00:47:05,633
- Oh darn, forgot my Chapstick.

1337
00:47:05,633 --> 00:47:07,400
Whatever.

1338
00:47:07,400 --> 00:47:09,167
I'm telling you,
Blixen, he's gained

1339
00:47:09,167 --> 00:47:10,900
about 30 pounds since last year.

1340
00:47:10,900 --> 00:47:12,233
I don't think I can hold out.

1341
00:47:12,233 --> 00:47:15,933
(Panting)

1342
00:47:15,933 --> 00:47:17,500
- Uh, this is Houston, Santa.

1343
00:47:17,500 --> 00:47:19,033
We're tracking you on radar.

1344
00:47:19,033 --> 00:47:20,900
Seem to be having some trouble
there with the primary thrust

1345
00:47:20,900 --> 00:47:21,900
system.

1346
00:47:21,900 --> 00:47:23,800
Uh, repeat, eject now.

1347
00:47:23,800 --> 00:47:25,267
- Uh-oh.

1348
00:47:25,267 --> 00:47:26,800
Santa got drunk and delivered
all the gifts to the moon

1349
00:47:26,800 --> 00:47:28,933
again.

1350
00:47:28,933 --> 00:47:30,067
- Whew, that was close.

1351
00:47:30,067 --> 00:47:31,067
- Well, no.

1352
00:47:31,067 --> 00:47:33,033
- He almost ran into the moon.

1353
00:47:33,033 --> 00:47:34,300
- Just take my word for it.

1354
00:47:37,167 --> 00:47:38,733
- And here's the planet Earth.

1355
00:47:38,733 --> 00:47:39,933
- Well, kind of.

1356
00:47:39,933 --> 00:47:42,200
- I wonder where
Santa will go first.

1357
00:47:42,200 --> 00:47:43,300
Europe?

1358
00:47:43,300 --> 00:47:44,467
Africa?

1359
00:47:44,467 --> 00:47:45,300
America?

1360
00:47:45,300 --> 00:47:46,567
- Ripple pines?

1361
00:47:49,233 --> 00:47:51,267
(singing) I like
to live in America.

1362
00:47:51,267 --> 00:47:52,567
Cadillacs zoom in America.

1363
00:47:57,200 --> 00:47:59,733
- Think of all the nice things
you'll get from Santa Claus.

1364
00:47:59,733 --> 00:48:01,433
- Yes, Mama.

1365
00:48:01,433 --> 00:48:02,433
- That's a good boy.

1366
00:48:02,433 --> 00:48:03,367
- Or a girl.

1367
00:48:03,367 --> 00:48:04,567
- See you in the morning.

1368
00:48:04,567 --> 00:48:05,567
- If you get bored,
you can go down

1369
00:48:05,567 --> 00:48:07,500
and practice your piano lesson.

1370
00:48:07,500 --> 00:48:09,333
See you later, my darling.

1371
00:48:09,333 --> 00:48:10,333
- Our love's implied.

1372
00:48:10,333 --> 00:48:11,533
Goodbye.

1373
00:48:11,533 --> 00:48:12,467
Maybe we can do
this again sometime.

1374
00:48:12,467 --> 00:48:14,967
You seem like a nice kid.

1375
00:48:14,967 --> 00:48:16,200
- Ugh.

1376
00:48:16,200 --> 00:48:19,067
Why do they leave me
so heavily medicated?

1377
00:48:19,067 --> 00:48:23,000
Um, were... were my
parents just here?

1378
00:48:23,000 --> 00:48:26,600
If I could just get some
movement in my legs.

1379
00:48:26,600 --> 00:48:28,433
(Whimpering)

1380
00:48:31,233 --> 00:48:32,433
- I knew it.

1381
00:48:32,433 --> 00:48:34,367
The Devil is nearby,
and these three

1382
00:48:34,367 --> 00:48:36,700
certainly are up to no good.

1383
00:48:36,700 --> 00:48:37,967
- OK, listen now.

1384
00:48:37,967 --> 00:48:39,433
As soon as Santa Claus lands

1385
00:48:39,433 --> 00:48:41,233
on the roof here,
all three of us

1386
00:48:41,233 --> 00:48:42,667
will jump on him.

1387
00:48:42,667 --> 00:48:44,633
We'll tie him up and
we'll stick him in a sack.

1388
00:48:44,633 --> 00:48:47,400
And then we'll go home
with all of Santa's toys.

1389
00:48:47,400 --> 00:48:49,067
- But what about Santa?

1390
00:48:49,067 --> 00:48:51,767
- We can make him our slave,
and all of the candies and toys

1391
00:48:51,767 --> 00:48:52,967
will belong to us.

1392
00:48:52,967 --> 00:48:54,200
- Gee, nice kids.

1393
00:48:54,200 --> 00:48:55,133
- So whenever we
want something...

1394
00:48:55,133 --> 00:48:56,900
- Oh boy, this is gonna be fun.

1395
00:48:56,900 --> 00:48:57,900
- Better not talk now.

1396
00:48:57,900 --> 00:49:00,500
He can hear, so get away.

1397
00:49:00,500 --> 00:49:02,833
- Isn't kidnapping
Santa a federal offense?

1398
00:49:02,833 --> 00:49:05,600
- I think so.

1399
00:49:05,600 --> 00:49:07,600
- No, a strolling Gallagher.

1400
00:49:07,600 --> 00:49:08,933
- Ugh.

1401
00:49:08,933 --> 00:49:12,300
(Music playing)

1402
00:49:12,300 --> 00:49:14,400
- It's a Fellini Christmas.

1403
00:49:14,400 --> 00:49:16,267
(Music playing)

1404
00:49:16,267 --> 00:49:17,267
- Attica!

1405
00:49:17,267 --> 00:49:17,933
Attica!

1406
00:49:17,933 --> 00:49:19,200
- Time for bed.

1407
00:49:19,200 --> 00:49:21,533
Santa Claus will be
here any minute now.

1408
00:49:21,533 --> 00:49:24,233
- Mama, and who is Santa Claus?

1409
00:49:24,233 --> 00:49:26,800
- He's the man in the store,
the one with the red suit

1410
00:49:26,800 --> 00:49:29,333
and the white beard that
was laughing very much.

1411
00:49:29,333 --> 00:49:31,300
- And does Santa know about me?

1412
00:49:31,300 --> 00:49:32,300
- Uh-huh.

1413
00:49:32,300 --> 00:49:35,733
- Is he real, like my daddy?

1414
00:49:35,733 --> 00:49:36,933
- No, not really.

1415
00:49:36,933 --> 00:49:39,333
- Would you shut the
bloody organ grinder up?

1416
00:49:39,333 --> 00:49:41,033
- Probably French.

1417
00:49:41,033 --> 00:49:42,367
- Hey.

1418
00:49:42,367 --> 00:49:44,133
- And comes here once a year.

1419
00:49:44,133 --> 00:49:45,900
- Who does he come for?

1420
00:49:45,900 --> 00:49:48,700
- They say he gives those to
children who are obedient.

1421
00:49:48,700 --> 00:49:50,267
- I don't think he likes me.

1422
00:49:50,267 --> 00:49:53,800
He has never brought
me any dollies.

1423
00:49:53,800 --> 00:49:54,800
- It's...

1424
00:49:54,800 --> 00:49:55,467
- He's just jealous.

1425
00:49:55,467 --> 00:49:57,733
not that.

1426
00:49:57,733 --> 00:49:59,533
Maybe you're forgetting
to ask him for dollies.

1427
00:49:59,533 --> 00:50:00,533
- Yeah, bull!

1428
00:50:00,533 --> 00:50:04,467
- And if I ask him for one now?

1429
00:50:04,467 --> 00:50:05,467
- Go ahead.

1430
00:50:05,467 --> 00:50:06,933
- Make my day.

1431
00:50:06,933 --> 00:50:08,900
- Perhaps he'll hear you.

1432
00:50:08,900 --> 00:50:10,967
We can say a prayer, dear.

1433
00:50:10,967 --> 00:50:12,667
- Mama, please don't cry.

1434
00:50:12,667 --> 00:50:13,667
- You will stain my dress.

1435
00:50:13,667 --> 00:50:16,200
- It's just that it's Christmas.

1436
00:50:16,200 --> 00:50:19,700
And Christmas always
makes me feel sad.

1437
00:50:19,700 --> 00:50:21,967
- You and a lot of other people.

1438
00:50:21,967 --> 00:50:25,567
- Mommy, what is
Christmas good for.

1439
00:50:25,567 --> 00:50:29,533
- Well, to remind us that
Christ was born many years ago.

1440
00:50:29,533 --> 00:50:30,900
- Craig?

1441
00:50:30,900 --> 00:50:32,133
- I don't think so.

1442
00:50:32,133 --> 00:50:34,200
- And he was even
poorer than we are.

1443
00:50:34,200 --> 00:50:35,200
- Whoa.

1444
00:50:35,200 --> 00:50:36,833
- He was born in a bed of straw.

1445
00:50:36,833 --> 00:50:37,833
- Know what, Mama?

1446
00:50:37,833 --> 00:50:39,300
- I don't buy it.

1447
00:50:39,300 --> 00:50:41,433
- I already asked Santa
Claus for two pretty dollies.

1448
00:50:41,433 --> 00:50:45,533
If he brings me two, I'll
give one to little Jesus.

1449
00:50:45,533 --> 00:50:47,800
- Oh, he's got plenty
of presents already.

1450
00:50:47,800 --> 00:50:49,967
- Yes, my darling.

1451
00:50:49,967 --> 00:50:53,700
Maye if we pray with
all of our might, hmm?

1452
00:50:53,700 --> 00:50:54,700
- Oh, look at that.

1453
00:50:54,700 --> 00:50:55,667
The roof's leaking.

1454
00:50:55,667 --> 00:50:57,433
I thought I spackled that.

1455
00:50:57,433 --> 00:50:59,367
(Christmas music)

1456
00:50:59,367 --> 00:51:02,400
- (singing) Shotgun
shells, BB's in the air.

1457
00:51:02,400 --> 00:51:03,967
If I don't find a break
in this cloud cover,

1458
00:51:03,967 --> 00:51:05,067
I'm never gonna make it.

1459
00:51:05,067 --> 00:51:06,067
(Music playing)

1460
00:51:06,067 --> 00:51:07,767
- Plink, plink, plink, plink.

1461
00:51:07,767 --> 00:51:09,833
Pizzicato plink, plink.

1462
00:51:09,833 --> 00:51:11,233
Come legato in.

1463
00:51:11,233 --> 00:51:13,167
- Knick-knack, paddywhack,
give a dog a bone.

1464
00:51:13,167 --> 00:51:15,500
- While Santa steers his
sleigh towards Earth...

1465
00:51:15,500 --> 00:51:16,733
- Disaster awaits.

1466
00:51:16,733 --> 00:51:20,600
- Old devil Pitch
awaits his arrival.

1467
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:22,133
Here comes Santa now.

1468
00:51:22,133 --> 00:51:24,367
First stop, Mexico City.

1469
00:51:24,367 --> 00:51:26,033
- Manure dust
overtakes the sleigh.

1470
00:51:29,967 --> 00:51:32,367
- Oh, Santa, I need
some stuff, man.

1471
00:51:32,367 --> 00:51:33,367
Just a taste.

1472
00:51:33,367 --> 00:51:34,500
Come on, man.

1473
00:51:34,500 --> 00:51:36,000
- It's freezing.

1474
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:39,367
I wish I were back in
Hades, tending the furnaces.

1475
00:51:39,367 --> 00:51:41,567
(Santa laughing)

1476
00:51:41,567 --> 00:51:42,800
- He's heard Santa.

1477
00:51:42,800 --> 00:51:46,367
- Well, I hope so,
with ears like that.

1478
00:51:46,367 --> 00:51:47,900
- Boy, he's really hauling ass.

1479
00:51:47,900 --> 00:51:50,100
- And it's his.

1480
00:51:50,100 --> 00:51:51,733
- By Satan, there he is.

1481
00:51:51,733 --> 00:51:53,700
I'm committed and
I'm prepared to upset

1482
00:51:53,700 --> 00:51:54,700
his own merry Christmas.

1483
00:51:54,700 --> 00:51:55,833
Heh, heh.

1484
00:51:55,833 --> 00:51:56,833
- I love my work.

1485
00:51:56,833 --> 00:51:58,433
- We will see who wins out.

1486
00:51:58,433 --> 00:52:01,333
This is one night that
no one can take from me.

1487
00:52:01,333 --> 00:52:04,333
- He has kind of
an oily complexion.

1488
00:52:05,400 --> 00:52:06,667
- What's he going to do?

1489
00:52:06,667 --> 00:52:07,767
- You tell us.

1490
00:52:07,767 --> 00:52:09,067
- Oh-ho.

1491
00:52:09,067 --> 00:52:10,300
He's going to push
the chimney out

1492
00:52:10,300 --> 00:52:13,433
of place so that
poor old Santa won't

1493
00:52:13,433 --> 00:52:14,867
be able to enter this house.

1494
00:52:14,867 --> 00:52:16,433
- Well, that nut.

1495
00:52:16,433 --> 00:52:19,000
(Chuckling)

1496
00:52:19,000 --> 00:52:23,100
- I love Ron Reagan Jr.

1497
00:52:23,100 --> 00:52:24,100
- Hmm.

1498
00:52:24,100 --> 00:52:25,467
Satan, honey, no.

1499
00:52:25,467 --> 00:52:26,467
Ooh.

1500
00:52:26,467 --> 00:52:27,200
- Don't ever do that again.

1501
00:52:30,100 --> 00:52:32,533
(Vomiting noise)

1502
00:52:32,533 --> 00:52:35,167
- (singing) The
Devil is a wiener.

1503
00:52:35,167 --> 00:52:38,033
Wiener, wiener, wiener.

1504
00:52:38,033 --> 00:52:41,500
- Well, I'll park in
the ramp this time.

1505
00:52:41,500 --> 00:52:42,533
- Don't do that with your hands.

1506
00:52:42,533 --> 00:52:43,533
Don't.

1507
00:52:43,533 --> 00:52:48,533
(Christmas music)

1508
00:52:49,000 --> 00:52:50,000
- Oof.

1509
00:52:54,000 --> 00:52:56,967
(Helicopter sounds)

1510
00:52:56,967 --> 00:52:58,600
- So this is all the
toys in the world

1511
00:52:58,600 --> 00:53:00,067
for all the children
in the world?

1512
00:53:00,067 --> 00:53:00,967
- Yep.

1513
00:53:03,033 --> 00:53:04,633
- Hefty, hefty, hefty.

1514
00:53:04,633 --> 00:53:06,133
- Wimpy, wimpy, wimpy.

1515
00:53:11,433 --> 00:53:12,800
- Oh, come on.

1516
00:53:12,800 --> 00:53:14,867
This is a very difficult
move for this actor.

1517
00:53:18,833 --> 00:53:19,833
- You know what, Santa?

1518
00:53:19,833 --> 00:53:20,800
It's about 4:00 AM.

1519
00:53:20,800 --> 00:53:24,667
You'd better get a rush on.

1520
00:53:24,667 --> 00:53:25,667
- Ugh.

1521
00:53:25,667 --> 00:53:26,567
Ugh.

1522
00:53:26,567 --> 00:53:27,500
- Terpsichore.

1523
00:53:29,900 --> 00:53:32,400
- Whew, that was
some action sequence.

1524
00:53:32,400 --> 00:53:33,900
Whew.

1525
00:53:33,900 --> 00:53:35,633
- He's got a Stephen King
manuscript in that bag.

1526
00:53:35,633 --> 00:53:40,467
- Let's hope Santa
realizes what's happened.

1527
00:53:40,467 --> 00:53:41,900
(Grunting)

1528
00:53:41,900 --> 00:53:42,900
- Oops.

1529
00:53:42,900 --> 00:53:46,300
- Well, what's happened here?

1530
00:53:46,300 --> 00:53:47,567
I can smell sulfur.

1531
00:53:47,567 --> 00:53:48,567
- Oh, sorry, that was me.

1532
00:53:48,567 --> 00:53:50,267
- Well, that must explain this.

1533
00:53:50,267 --> 00:53:52,567
That old devil Pitch
must be around here.

1534
00:53:55,200 --> 00:53:56,700
(Grunting)

1535
00:53:56,700 --> 00:53:59,367
- Jim J. Bullock is more
frightening than that devil.

1536
00:53:59,367 --> 00:54:00,400
- Hi, Mr. Rush.

1537
00:54:03,333 --> 00:54:05,533
- Santa's determined to get in.

1538
00:54:05,533 --> 00:54:07,100
He'll find a way.

1539
00:54:07,100 --> 00:54:08,567
He's not one to give up.

1540
00:54:11,433 --> 00:54:13,533
- O-ho, got some
plastique in here.

1541
00:54:13,533 --> 00:54:17,033
Fragmentation bomb.

1542
00:54:17,033 --> 00:54:20,200
- Well, time for a Mai Tai.

1543
00:54:20,200 --> 00:54:22,167
Big one, too.

1544
00:54:22,167 --> 00:54:24,700
- Well, there's more than
one way to beat the Devil.

1545
00:54:24,700 --> 00:54:27,333
Santa will jump down
using his magic parasol.

1546
00:54:27,333 --> 00:54:30,200
- With a 10-point
degree of difficulty.

1547
00:54:30,200 --> 00:54:32,400
- Old Pitch hadn't
counted on this.

1548
00:54:32,400 --> 00:54:33,400
- Doh!

1549
00:54:33,400 --> 00:54:34,333
- He's almost green with anger.

1550
00:54:37,433 --> 00:54:42,400
- And it took a fly gang
of 16 to lower Santa down.

1551
00:54:43,833 --> 00:54:47,267
- Tuck and roll,
Kringle, tuck and roll.

1552
00:54:47,267 --> 00:54:48,267
- I'm frustrated.

1553
00:54:51,100 --> 00:54:52,100
- He's good.

1554
00:54:54,133 --> 00:54:58,400
(Alarm sounds)

1555
00:55:01,700 --> 00:55:04,933
- It is the witching
hour, my friend.

1556
00:55:04,933 --> 00:55:06,467
- Uh-oh.

1557
00:55:06,467 --> 00:55:11,000
These two seem to know that
Santa's in the living room.

1558
00:55:11,000 --> 00:55:13,067
Look out, Santa,
they'll see you.

1559
00:55:13,067 --> 00:55:16,300
(Sound of shotgun
racking and firing)

1560
00:55:16,300 --> 00:55:17,533
- Yeah.

1561
00:55:17,533 --> 00:55:19,800
Well, that's the last
thing they'll ever see.

1562
00:55:19,800 --> 00:55:20,800
- Why, of course.

1563
00:55:20,800 --> 00:55:23,033
Santa can handle this.

1564
00:55:23,033 --> 00:55:25,633
All he has to do is
use the magic dreaming

1565
00:55:25,633 --> 00:55:27,567
powders prepared by Mr. Merlin.

1566
00:55:27,567 --> 00:55:30,333
- And Mr. Owsley.

1567
00:55:30,333 --> 00:55:34,000
- And it isn't long before
our two little stay-up-lates

1568
00:55:34,000 --> 00:55:36,100
are sleeping soundly
in their bed.

1569
00:55:36,100 --> 00:55:38,967
- Unfortunately, the powder
does have contraindications

1570
00:55:38,967 --> 00:55:41,600
and enduring side effects.

1571
00:55:41,600 --> 00:55:42,833
(Music playing)

1572
00:55:42,833 --> 00:55:44,200
- (singing) It's
the Devil's theme.

1573
00:55:44,200 --> 00:55:46,333
He's doing a little song.

1574
00:55:46,333 --> 00:55:48,500
Even though he's the
embodiment of evil,

1575
00:55:48,500 --> 00:55:50,767
he's still got a goofy song.

1576
00:55:50,767 --> 00:55:53,767
In his tights he brings
death, despair, disruption,

1577
00:55:53,767 --> 00:55:55,000
and disease.

1578
00:55:55,000 --> 00:55:59,067
Now let's all join him,
and I'll laugh along.

1579
00:55:59,067 --> 00:56:00,133
Devil.

1580
00:56:00,133 --> 00:56:01,600
- Now what?

1581
00:56:01,600 --> 00:56:04,400
Must be Pitch putting the
chimney back in place.

1582
00:56:04,400 --> 00:56:07,767
- Son of a... this time I'm
putting my patent leather shoe

1583
00:56:07,767 --> 00:56:08,767
down... permanently.

1584
00:56:11,033 --> 00:56:12,267
- Ha.

1585
00:56:12,267 --> 00:56:13,233
This year I gave
everyone Yahtzee.

1586
00:56:19,367 --> 00:56:20,367
(Vomiting sound)

1587
00:56:25,800 --> 00:56:26,800
- Ha, ha.

1588
00:56:30,267 --> 00:56:31,767
- Hey, pitch black.

1589
00:56:31,767 --> 00:56:32,767
Ha.

1590
00:56:32,767 --> 00:56:34,167
Because of the...

1591
00:56:34,167 --> 00:56:35,567
- It's a living.

1592
00:56:35,567 --> 00:56:37,000
Huh.

1593
